{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340966",
      "title": "Invalidating Custom Data Source Data",
      "lectureOrder": 191,
      "videoOrder": 177,
      "sourceHash": "f8d451a5b1e64d1ddbc5a0a4ebd4531d154bbcc12da8a2f3173557fcb4aa9204",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 2.13,
          "en": "So you did now learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 6.57,
          "en": "how you can cache data from your own data source.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.57,
          "end": 8.61,
          "en": "However, now that we added this caching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.61,
          "end": 11.16,
          "en": "we'll face a problem even during development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.16,
          "end": 15.78,
          "en": "If I now add a new fourth message, it doesn't appear here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.78,
          "end": 19.14,
          "en": "A problem we previously only faced in production",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.14,
          "end": 21.87,
          "en": "due to that full route cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 24.57,
          "en": "Now, since we set up this cache here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.57,
          "end": 28.23,
          "en": "and hence we got this data cache, we got the same problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.23,
          "end": 31.53,
          "en": "if you want to call it like this, during development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.53,
          "end": 32.91,
          "en": "But it's not actually a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.91,
          "end": 37.08,
          "en": "Instead, it's the behavior NextJS has out of the box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.08,
          "end": 39.66,
          "en": "it caches aggressively.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.66,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "What we have to do to see our data again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 44.82,
          "en": "is we have to tell NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.82,
          "end": 48.24,
          "en": "that the data that's cached here did change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.24,
          "end": 50.97,
          "en": "And how can we tell NextJS?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.97,
          "end": 54.66,
          "en": "Well, there are essentially two main ways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 57.51,
          "en": "In the place where we create that new data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.51,
          "end": 61.02,
          "en": "we can call that revalidatePath function again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.02,
          "end": 63.033,
          "en": "and we saw that function before already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.9,
          "end": 65.07,
          "en": "And I can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.07,
          "end": 68.55,
          "en": "revalidate the data on /messages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.55,
          "end": 71.31,
          "en": "With that any cached data used on this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.31,
          "end": 73.86,
          "en": "will be thrown away and will be re-fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.86,
          "end": 76.47,
          "en": "whenever this function here was called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.47,
          "end": 78.66,
          "en": "So right after adding a new message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.66,
          "end": 81.63,
          "en": "I'm calling this function to tell NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.63,
          "end": 84.36,
          "en": "that any data and the full route cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.36,
          "end": 87.72,
          "en": "of the /messages page should be thrown away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.72,
          "end": 89.4,
          "en": "and the data should be re-fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.4,
          "end": 91.95,
          "en": "and the page should be re-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.95,
          "end": 93.9,
          "en": "Therefore, with this added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 93.9,
          "end": 96,
          "en": "I still don't see the message if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 96,
          "end": 98.31,
          "en": "but now for every new message we add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.31,
          "end": 99.78,
          "en": "the cache will be cleared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 99.78,
          "end": 103.768,
          "en": "and hence, any new messages now will show up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.768,
          "end": 105.75,
          "en": "As you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.75,
          "end": 108.24000000000001,
          "en": "So that's one way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.24000000000001,
          "end": 111.96000000000001,
          "en": "Now, an alternative to calling revalidatePath",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.96000000000001,
          "end": 114.47999999999999,
          "en": "and revalidate the data that's attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 118.68,
          "en": "to a specific page is to instead call revalidateTag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 121.563,
          "en": "and add a tag to the cached data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.4,
          "end": 125.31,
          "en": "And you can add a tag to cached data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.31,
          "end": 127.11,
          "en": "when using unstable_cache,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.11,
          "end": 130.5,
          "en": "which I renamed to nextCache here in my case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.5,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "by passing a third argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 135.21,
          "en": "to this unstable_cache function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.21,
          "end": 138.72,
          "en": "And that third argument is a configuration object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.72,
          "end": 142.14,
          "en": "which allows you to set up two different settings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 142.14,
          "end": 145.95,
          "en": "With revalidate, you could set up a time period,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 145.95,
          "end": 148.2,
          "en": "in seconds again, after which the cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.2,
          "end": 150.18,
          "en": "would always be re-validate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 150.18,
          "end": 152.82,
          "en": "So that would be another way of re-setting it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 152.82,
          "end": 157.2,
          "en": "or re-fetching. But here I'm looking for the tags setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.2,
          "end": 159.54,
          "en": "And this then takes an array of tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 159.54,
          "end": 161.57999999999998,
          "en": "which are totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 161.57999999999998,
          "end": 163.77,
          "en": "So you can add as many tags as you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 163.77,
          "end": 166.44299999999998,
          "en": "and any tag values of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 167.73,
          "end": 172.2,
          "en": "That will then add those tags to this cached data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 176.37,
          "en": "And if you then call revalidateTag with one of these tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.37,
          "end": 178.26,
          "en": "that data will be thrown away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.26,
          "end": 181.17,
          "en": "and any place in your NextJS application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 181.17,
          "end": 184.86,
          "en": "any page layout or component that fetches data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 184.86,
          "end": 187.92,
          "en": "from that data source with that tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 191.34,
          "en": "will be re-executed and the respective page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 191.34,
          "end": 194.16,
          "en": "and component will be re-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 195.9,
          "en": "So with this setup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 195.9,
          "end": 199.5,
          "en": "if I now add a new message here like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 199.5,
          "end": 201.188,
          "en": "that message also shows up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 201.188,
          "end": 203.853,
          "en": "because we're using revalidateTag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 204.99,
          "end": 208.23,
          "en": "And that's how you can invalidate the cache data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 208.23,
          "end": 210.393,
          "en": "when managing the cache on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
